          "title": "Why Short Reviews Help",
          "prompt": "글의 중심 생각으로 가장 적절한 것은?",
          "passage": "Many students read a new word several times and feel certain that they know it. However, seeing a word is not the same as recalling it without help. A short quiz can reveal what the learner can actually remember. Reviewing the same material on different days also offers a useful challenge: the learner must bring the information back after some forgetting has occurred. This does not mean every review should be difficult. When a student makes a mistake, a clear explanation and another chance to answer can make the next attempt more useful. Over time, a series of short reviews may be easier to maintain than one very long study session.",
